# Maintainer: Jordan Bettcher <thebettcher@gmail.com>
#
# The Dart SDK on ppc64le (POWER8+, little-endian, ELFv2, glibc), with a
# native ppc64 VM backend -- JIT and AOT -- carried as a patch series:
# the dart CLI and its tools (pub, analyze, format, compile exe/aot-snapshot/
# kernel/js/wasm, test, doc, DDS), dartvm, dartaotruntime, gen_snapshot and
# the core libraries, installed as /usr/lib/dart with /usr/bin/dart and
# /usr/bin/dartaotruntime.
#
# Class: local workaround (distribution packaging: system toolchain, no
# gclient, CIPD client or sysroot). The port itself is classified patch by
# patch in the table below.
#
# Seven things about this build are worth knowing before changing it.
#
# 1. THE PORT IS A PERMANENT DOWNSTREAM CARRY. Upstream adds architectures only
#    when it will maintain them itself (mraleph on dart-lang/sdk#63407, the
#    LoongArch backend, rejected May 2026). The numbered NNNN-*.patch files
#    beside this PKGBUILD are the series' one durable home: `git format-patch`
#    output of the unpublished port branch (flutter-port work/dart-ppc64,
#    ppc64-backend), exported with dart-ppc64-export-patches.sh and copied in
#    by ./sync-series. Each is applied with `patch -Np1` from the SDK root,
#    including the ones for the BoringSSL and dart-lang/native DEPS
#    checkouts. flutter-engine applies the same files (symlinks, its
#    sync-dart-series) to the Dart inside the engine; gate D there proves it
#    is the same source as this package.
#
# 2. SOURCES ARE FETCHED IN prepare(), SHALLOW, BY COMMIT ID, as in
#    flutter-engine: the SDK at the 3.11.5 tag, then the 39 git DEPS
#    (dart-sdk-fetch.sh, beside this file: one `git fetch --depth 1 <url>
#    <sha>` each, checked against its pin). makepkg git+ sources would be
#    `git clone --mirror`s, 5.2 GiB for the SDK repo alone (flutter-engine
#    REPORT). Real git checkouts are also what tools/make_version.py reads for
#    the version string and SDK hash. Of the 19 CIPD DEPS only devtools is
#    shipped (bin/resources/devtools); it is a checksummed source from CIPD's
#    plain /dl/ endpoint. The rest are toolchains, sysroots and test data,
#    replaced by system packages or unused. bq shares the host's network
#    namespace (flutter-port R15), so fetching in prepare() works under bq.
#
# 3. GATES. Each hashes a tree with git (`add -A -f; write-tree`), every
#    DEPS path excluded except where named:
#      gate 1  the SDK checkout is the tag (_base_tree)
#      gate 2  the SDK after the series == _tree, the port branch's tree
#      deps    each DEPS checkout the series touches == _dep_trees[path]
#    The series is exact: applied to the pristine pins it reproduces the port
#    branch byte for byte, so the package provably builds the source the
#    port was tested on (ours/webkit's rule).
#
# 4. DART IS SELF-HOSTING. The build runs a prebuilt Dart from
#    tools/sdks/dart-sdk, a symlink to /usr/lib/dart-bootstrap, to compile
#    the tree's own pkg/ sources: gen_kernel, compile_platform, dart2js,
#    create_snapshot_entry -- front-end work whose output (kernel, JS,
#    Dart source) is platform-independent. Every snapshot that holds machine
#    code is made by the gen_snapshot/dartvm this build compiles. CONTROL
#    checks, in prepare() before the DEPS hooks first run the driver and
#    again in build(), refuse a driver that is not a native linux_ppc64 Dart
#    from this pool, and a build graph that runs the prebuilt for anything
#    but those programs, asks it for a non-kernel snapshot, or runs a binary
#    from outside the tree. _driver=system uses the pool's previous `dart`
#    instead (N -> N+1 version hops). dart-bootstrap's header has the
#    provenance chain back to the emulated arm64 stage 0.
#
# 5. CODEGEN IS POWER8 IN BOTH POOLS, C++ IS PER POOL. The backend has no
#    ISA 3.0 emitter, so JIT code and every AOT snapshot -- the SDK's own
#    tools, `dart compile` output, every Flutter app's libapp.so -- are ISA
#    2.07 whichever pool built them; build() gates the AOT snapshots at 0
#    ISA 3.0 instructions in BOTH pools. _power8_compat selects only the
#    C/C++ -mcpu of the VM binaries, through the GN arg ppc64_cpu (series
#    0004; GN never reads CFLAGS), asserted on every compile. In the baseline
#    pool every installed ELF must scan 0. In the POWER9 pool the VM binaries
#    carry ISA 3.0 by design (-mcpu=power9, plus the POWER9 pool's static
#    libstdc++/libsupc++/libgcc: 1,197 words even with the compiler-default
#    -mcpu, measured by M5); they are counted into .pkginfo, not gated.
#
# 6. bq RUNS makepkg --nocheck. Every gate is in prepare() or build(); check()
#    is for a native, by-hand makepkg. Inside bq, /usr is a read-only overlay
#    and $HOME is the real home, so HOME, PUB_CACHE and XDG_CONFIG_HOME point
#    into $srcdir. package() runs under fakeroot and only copies files.
#
# 7. BUILD THIS NATIVELY: through bq / tools/build-ppc64le.sh, or makepkg in a
#    native shell, never inside the POWERarm aarch64 sleeve Claude sessions
#    run in (fakeroot there half-works and produces -rw------- packages owned
#    by the builder). An agent reaches the native shell with:
#    ssh -n -i ~/.ssh/id_claude_omarchy -o BatchMode=yes localhost
#    Put the build root on /mnt/arch (BQ_BUILDROOT): ~3 GiB of sources and
#    ~14 GiB of out/.
#
# Reproducibility, measured 2026-11-19: two independent builds of this recipe
# (same build path) gave packages identical in 999 of 1,000 files; the one
# that differed is an app-jit snapshot (analysis_server). The three app-jit
# snapshots (analysis_server, dartdevc, kernel-service) come from a timed JIT
# training run and may differ on any build; nothing gates their bytes. The
# 14 AOT/app-jit snapshots embed the build tree's absolute path (file://
# URIs), which is what makepkg's "Package contains reference to $srcdir"
# warning is about; bq's elf-pathguard tolerates build-tree paths inside ELF
# files (only $SYSROOT paths fail), so the warning is expected.
#
# PKGREL RULE. pacman compares versions, not contents: bump pkgrel whenever
# the series, the gates or this recipe change at the same pkgver, then bump
# flutter-engine (it embeds this VM) and everything built with `dart`.
#
# THE PATCH SERIES, in order (generated by ./sync-series from each patch's
# own Class: line, or series.class where the commit message has none):
# BEGIN generated: sync-series classes
# 0001 [ppc64] tools: accept a ppc64le host; take the host arch from --host-arch
#      Class: upstreamable in form (the --host-arch override is useful on any
#        emulated build host); the ppc64 entries only matter together with the
#        out-of-tree ppc64 backend.
# 0002 [ppc64] runtime: HOST_ARCH_PPC64 host plumbing
#      Class: upstreamable in form; only useful upstream together with a ppc64
#        backend, which upstream does not take (dart-lang/sdk#63407).
# 0003 [ppc64] smith: add the ppc64 architecture; map a ppc64le host to it
#      Class: needed locally to run tools/test.py-style suites on this host;
#        upstreamable only together with the ppc64 backend.
# 0004 [ppc64] build: add the ppc64 cpu to the GN build
#      Class: upstreamable in form (same shape as the riscv64 enablement); the
#        toolchain is only exercised with the ppc64 port.
# 0005 [ppc64] build: system clang/lld and no Debian sysroot where CIPD has none
#      Class: local workaround (distribution packaging) in purpose; the two
#        stamp conditions are upstreamable bug fixes on their own.
# 0006 [ppc64] runtime: 64 KiB page constants for Linux/PPC64, as for Linux/ARM64
#      Class: upstreamable fix (the predicate is useful even without a ppc64
#        backend, e.g. for future 64 KiB-page targets).
# 0007 [ppc64] sync the backend components into the tree
#      Class: local carry: the backend itself, new files only (assembler,
#        disassembler, IL, flow graph compiler, stubs, constants); the hunks
#        to the shared locations.h and stub_code_compiler.cc are its arch arms
# 0008 [ppc64] runtime: TARGET_ARCH_PPC64 arms, GN wiring, code patterns
#      Class: local carry: backend enablement (TARGET_ARCH_PPC64 arms, GN
#        wiring, ELF EM_PPC64/EF_PPC64_ABI_V2, assembly-snapshot CFI);
#        upstreamable in form only together with the backend
# 0009 [ppc64] sync the backend components into the tree
#      Class: local carry: the ELFv2 FFI (Abi.linuxPpc64 in pkg/vm and the VM,
#        marshaller and native calling convention); its
#        runtime/vm/compiler/ffi/unit_test.cc and unit_test_custom_zone.h
#        hunks are the clang 22 / libstdc++ include fix, upstreamable on its
#        own (UPSTREAM-CANDIDATES, IL-C ffi/0002)
# 0010 [ppc64] runtime: offsets for TARGET_ARCH_PPC64
#      Class: local carry: generated runtime offsets for TARGET_ARCH_PPC64,
#        extracted natively (tools/run_offsets_extractor.dart cannot cross-
#        build ppc64)
# 0011 [ppc64] runtime: DWARF CFI for ppc64
#      Class: upstreamable in form: DWARF CFI uses DW_CFA_offset_extended for
#        registers >= 64 (ELFv2's LR is 65); no change for any existing
#        architecture
# 0012 [ppc64] sync the backend components into the tree
#      Class: local carry: backend (assembler, IL, flow graph compiler, FFI
#        calling convention, cpu_ppc64)
# 0013 [ppc64] sync the backend components into the tree
#      Class: local carry: backend; the flow_graph_compiler.cc hunk routes
#        kUnboxedFloat Dart stack slots through FpuTMP on ppc64 only (ABI-SPEC
#        A7)
# 0014 [ppc64] sync the backend components into the tree
#      Class: local carry: backend (il.h arch list)
# 0015 [ppc64] runtime: BareSwitchableCallPattern for the AOT switchable call
#      Class: local carry: backend, AOT switchable-call pattern decoder
# 0016 [ppc64] runtime: object_ppc64_test.cc
#      Class: local test harness: object_ppc64_test.cc code generators for
#        object_test.cc
# 0017 [ppc64] sync the backend components into the tree
#      Class: local carry: backend (flow graph compiler)
# 0018 [ppc64] runtime: list stub_code_ppc64_test.cc in vm_sources_tests
#      Class: local test harness: stub_code_ppc64_test.cc listed in
#        vm_sources_tests
# 0019 [ppc64] sync the backend components into the tree
#      Class: local carry: backend assembler and stub unit tests
# 0020 [ppc64] sync the backend components into the tree
#      Class: local carry: backend (assembler, instructions_ppc64 call
#        patterns); assembler_base.h gains the ppc64 arm
# 0021 [ppc64] sync the backend components into the tree
#      Class: local carry: backend (assembler, constants)
# 0022 [ppc64] sync the backend components into the tree
#      Class: local carry: backend (assembler + tests, IL)
# 0023 [ppc64] sync the backend components into the tree
#      Class: local carry: backend (cpu_ppc64: icache flush, HWCAP2 features)
# 0024 [ppc64] sync the backend components into the tree
#      Class: upstreamable fix + local carry: flow_graph_compiler.cc blocks
#        FpuTMP in AllocateRegistersLocally (latent on every arch whose FpuTMP
#        is not the last FPU register; UPSTREAM-CANDIDATES, il/shared 0002);
#        the marshaller.cc hunk is the ppc64 variadic-HFA saved copy
# 0025 [ppc64] sync the backend components into the tree
#      Class: local carry: pkg/vm native-assets validator knows the ppc64
#        architecture name
# 0026 [ppc64] sync the backend components into the tree
#      Class: local carry: backend (assembler, disassembler, stubs, constants,
#        stub tests)
# 0027 [ppc64] sync the backend components into the tree
#      Class: local test harness: relocation_test ppc64 arms; its "caller
#        poisons the result register" change is upstreamable for every arch
#        (UPSTREAM-CANDIDATES, aot 0001)
# 0028 [ppc64] sync the backend components into the tree
#      Class: local carry: pkg/native_stack_traces recognises EM_PPC64 as
#        "ppc64" (aot 0002), plus a stub_code_compiler_ppc64 fix
# 0029 [ppc64] sync the backend components into the tree
#      Class: upstreamable fix: linear-scan SpillAfter spilled register uses
#        between the loop header and the spill point; a latent miscompile on
#        every arch (release arm64 encodes a garbage register; UPSTREAM-
#        CANDIDATES, il/shared 0003)
# 0030 [ppc64] sync the backend components into the tree
#      Class: local test harness (aot 0004/0005/0007: vm.status SkipByDesign,
#        LLVM tools in buildtools/linux-ppc64, Mach-O legs skipped) + Mach-O
#        snapshots use 64 KiB pages on PPC64 (aot 0006; upstreamable as "size
#        Mach-O pages for the largest host page")
# 0031 [ppc64] runtime: build analyze_snapshot for ppc64
#      Class: local carry: runtime_args.gni builds analyze_snapshot for ppc64
#        (64-bit AOT runtime; Flutter's //flutter:flutter depends on it); a
#        one-line arch list, upstreamable only with the backend
# 0032 [ppc64] sync the backend components into the tree
#      Class: local carry: backend; code_patcher_ppc64.cc patches an AOT
#        switchable call (target, data) pair with the mutators stopped, since
#        ppc64 call sites read the pair with two independent loads (B's A17
#        race fix: SEGV in concurrent lazy-deopt tests)
# 0033 [ppc64] Add a ppc64le target (generic C, no assembly)
#      Class: local workaround for BoringSSL (upstream dropped ppc64le);
#        Debian chromium carries an equivalent, larger patch that also
#        restores the assembly.
# 0034 [ppc64] sync the backend components into third_party/pkg/native
#      Class: required, upstreamable to dart-lang/native once Dart has ppc64:
#        Architecture.ppc64 / Target.linuxPpc64 in third_party/pkg/native
#        code_assets and hooks_runner (ABI-SPEC A2, aot 0003); without it
#        every dartdev command fails
# END generated classes

pkgname=dart
pkgver=3.11.5
pkgrel=1
pkgdesc='Dart SDK: the dart CLI, JIT VM, AOT compiler and runtime, and core libraries (ppc64le port)'
arch=('powerpc64le')
url='https://dart.dev'
license=('BSD-3-Clause')

_url=https://dart.googlesource.com/sdk.git
_commit=c70f78e7d682c158c15ca0c26c729b3ccb932284   # tag 3.11.5
_commit_time='Wed Apr 15 00:36:32 2026 -0700'       # git log -1 --format=%cd 3.11.5
# The tag's tree: git rev-parse 3.11.5^{tree}. Also measured: the GitHub
# tarball of the tag, `git init; git add -A -f; git write-tree`, gives it.
_base_tree=6f9c66dab60de2381399ffb16dffa0ef6974c405
# Gate 2 and the DEPS gates: the port branch's trees, written by
# ./sync-series --trees-from <port repo> (flutter-port work/dart-ppc64,
# ppc64-backend dce83ce0, 2026-11-19 11:14). sync-series rewrites them.
_tree=c5aba92a8a98e5187a38d8942ffac4b1f186d428
# -g: makepkg sources this file inside a function, where a plain declare
# would make the array local to that function and empty by prepare().
declare -gA _dep_trees=(
  [third_party/boringssl/src]=a67ee71bb8c93180b9f6c516bcc92702db6b5b7a
  [third_party/pkg/native]=6b5e0cd25a6572ab51fb683632a2995c3dad5db1
)
_devtools_rev=9be2c887e3982e519cf58f185d5f7b008a4606e9

# Measured DT_NEEDED of dart, dartvm, dartaotruntime, gen_snapshot and
# wasm-opt (M5's create_sdk, 2026-11-19): libc.so.6, libm.so.6, ld64.so.2.
# The C++ runtime is linked statically.
depends=('glibc')
# Present on the host 2026-11-19: gn 0.2595 (M5 built with it), clang/lld/
# llvm 22.1.8, ninja 1.13.2, python 3.14.7, git 2.55. binutils for the
# objdump/readelf gates.
makedepends=('gn' 'clang' 'lld' 'llvm' 'ninja' 'python' 'git' 'patch' 'file' 'binutils')
provides=('dartaotruntime')
# !strip: create_sdk already installs stripped binaries (exe.stripped/), and
# bin/snapshots/*_aot.dart.snapshot are ELF files written by Dart's own ELF
# writer that strip would treat as libraries. !lto: GN ignores makepkg's flags.
options=('!strip' '!debug' '!lto')

# --- POWER8 / POWER9 ---------------------------------------------------------
# Set by tools/build-ppc64le.sh for the baseline pool. Selects ppc64_cpu (the
# VM's C/C++ -mcpu) and which pool's dart-bootstrap the CONTROL accepts.
_power8_compat=${_power8_compat:-0}
# One time only: the first baseline-pool dart has no baseline bootstrap yet.
# With this set it may be driven by the POWER9 dart-bootstrap, on the POWER9
# host, under tools/build-ppc64le.sh (so it links the baseline pool's own
# toolchain and libstdc++, and the baseline ISA gate applies); .pkginfo
# records it, and that package is what dart-bootstrap's baseline tarball is
# made from. Never on a POWER8 builder: the POWER9 bootstrap would SIGILL
# there, which is what the pool check prevents.
_cross_pool_bootstrap=${_cross_pool_bootstrap:-0}

# --- which Dart runs the front-end actions -----------------------------------
#   bootstrap  /usr/lib/dart-bootstrap (default)
#   system     /usr/lib/dart, the pool's previous dart package
#   external   $_driver_external, an extracted POWER9 dart-bootstrap package
#              (usr/lib/dart-bootstrap inside it). Only together with
#              _cross_pool_bootstrap=1: the baseline lane's sysroot cannot
#              stage the POWER9 package, and it must not enter repo-ppc64le.
#              bq binds / into its sandbox, so the path is visible there.
_driver=${_driver:-bootstrap}
case $_driver in
  bootstrap) _driver_sdk=/usr/lib/dart-bootstrap; makedepends+=("dart-bootstrap=$pkgver") ;;
  system)    _driver_sdk=/usr/lib/dart;           makedepends+=('dart') ;;
  external)  _driver_sdk=
             if (( _cross_pool_bootstrap )) && [[ ${_driver_external:-} == /* ]]; then
               _driver_sdk=$_driver_external
             fi ;;
  *)         _driver_sdk= ;;   # prepare() refuses
esac

